<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="gold-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="gold-title">Jewellers: gold moves without a sale</h2>
      <p>Gold goes to a karigar and returns as finished pieces, slightly lighter or with some loss. Customers bring old jewellery in exchange. Neither is a simple sale, and both can make stock look wrong.</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Keep a register by weight and purity for gold out and in</li>
        <li>Agree an allowed loss for each karigar in writing</li>
        <li>Show old gold received on the customer's bill</li>
        <li>Ask how section 143 of the CGST Act applies to goods with karigars</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Medicine and chemical traders</h2>
      <p>Goods with a shelf life need more than a quantity. Without batch and expiry details, you cannot tell what is about to lose its value, or answer a question about a sold lot.</p>
      <p class="para">Record expired goods when you remove them, and any return to the supplier. Ask how to treat tax credit already taken on goods written off. Licences for these trades are outside this page, but keep their costs and renewal dates on file.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="share-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="share-title">What every lane shares</h2>
      <p>Whatever you sell, old-market trade tends to mean party credit, family staff, and paper. Three habits help everywhere:</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Separate family withdrawals from business expenses</li>
        <li>Match each day's cash and UPI to the bills raised</li>
        <li>Photograph paper bills weekly, so a lost file is not a lost year</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="para">See {% routeLink "/industries/accounting-for-traders/", "accounting for traders" %} and {% routeLink "/guides/monthly-accounting-documents-checklist/", "the monthly documents checklist" %}.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Getting records out of the lanes</h2>
      <p>If you want someone to visit, ask how they will reach you and how often, since lanes and parking can make visits hard to keep up. If they work remotely, agree how bills will be scanned and sent.</p>
      <p class="para">AccountOrbit has no office in Chandni Chowk, and takes enquiries by phone from anywhere in Delhi. Naming them here explains the trades.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

